    "body": "- I like nested ternaries.\r\n- The second one is needed when you want to get the non-transformed stripped value. (basically, you get the stripped entity as a plain object)\r\n- `Object.keys` is used to check if the user has provided some `class-validator` options which means the returned object is a mutated version of `value` (stripped properties, etc.)",
